+   "severity": "minor",
+   "file": "apps/desktop/src/metaproject/MetaprojectTree.tsx",
+   "problem": "The dependency-less useLayoutEffect runs after every render. It calls rowElements() (querySelectorAll over every [data-row]) and then remember(document.activeElement), which calls rowElements() again plus indexOf. On a keystroke, moveTo and the row's onFocus -> remember each call rowElements() too. That is about four O(n) DOM queries and scans per arrow key, where before the fix round there were none unless a request was pending.",
+   "suggested_fix": "Reuse the `elements` array the layout effect already computed: remember(element, elements = rowElements()). In onFocus, take the index from rows.findIndex(r => r.id === row.id) instead of querying the DOM."
+  },
+  {
+   "id": "r2-clean-code-w2-F-001",
+   "severity": "minor",
+   "file": "apps/desktop/src/metaproject/MetaprojectTree.tsx",
+   "problem": "The component's doc comment describes the rule this fix round replaced. The new useLayoutEffect moves focus when data arrives: if the focused row (a Loading or Show more row) disappears because its folder's children or last page arrived, focus goes to the row now at its index (`elements[Math.min(lost.index, elements.length - 1)]?.focus()`). The tests added in this round assert exactly that (`a keyboard Retry keeps focus ... then on the first row read`: after `tree.release(\"src|\")`, `focused()` is `client.ts`). The doc still says focus moves only with the keyboard or a click and that data arriving never takes it; the inline comment at the effect states the narrower, correct rule ('Focus that was outside the tree is never taken').",
+   "suggested_fix": "Reword the doc to the rule the code now follows, e.g. 'Focus moves with the keyboard or a click. Data arriving never takes focus from outside the tree; when the focused row is replaced (its folder or next page loaded), focus goes to the row now at its place.'"
+  },
